---
title: Easy peanut butter cookies
servings: 18
yield: 18 cookies
tags: [quick]
cuisine: american
time: 15 minutes
source: Peanut Butter Cookies by John Kanell, Preppy Kitchen, https://preppykitchen.com/peanut-butter-cookies-recipe
nutrition:
  calories: 193 kcal
---

Heat the oven to 350°F.

Sift the @all-purpose flour{180%g} and @baking powder{3%g} together and whisk.

In a #stand mixer{} with the paddle, cream the @unsalted butter{113%g}, @light brown sugar{100%g}(lightly packed) and @granulated sugar{100%g}. Add the @?sea salt{1/4%tsp} now if using; up to 1/2 tsp.

Beat in the @peanut butter{250%g}, then the @egg{1}(room temperature) and @vanilla extract{5%ml}. Add the dry mix and beat until combined.

Roll into 1-inch balls, set them on a #baking sheet{} lined with parchment and press a criss-cross into each with a fork.

Bake ~{10%minutes}. Let them cool fully on the sheet; they firm up as they cool.
